---
import Welcome from "../components/Welcome.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

// Welcome to Astro! Wondering what to do next? Check out the Astro documentation at https://docs.astro.build
// Don't want to use any of this? Delete everything in this file, the `assets`, `components`, and `layouts` directories, and start fresh.
---

<Layout>
  <h1>Ferretboard</h1>
  <p>
    Ferretboard is a small games console running on a custom PCB with a rp2040
    chip and 240x240 screen.
  </p>
  <p>
    Created for <a href="https://macondo.hackclub.com/?ref=F2RS4">Hack Club Macondo</a> by <a
      href="https://new.louisbourgault.com">Louis Bourgault du Coudray</a>
  </p>
  <h2>Wasm Simulator (golang games system)</h2>
  <canvas id="canvas" width="240" height="240"></canvas>
  <script src="/wasm_exec.js" is:inline></script>
  <script>
    const go = new Go();
    WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming(fetch("main.wasm"), go.importObject)
      .then((result) => go.run(result.instance))
      .catch(console.error);
    let canvas = document.getElementById("canvas");
    const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
    ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;
  </script>
  <p class="game-instructions">Use WASD for d-pad buttons. Use J and K for A and B buttons, respectively. Use Enter for START and Shift for EXIT.</p>
  <p class="game-instructions">Press Shift (select) to exit any game</p>
  <h3>Controls for different games</h2>
  <details>
    <summary>Snake</summary>
    <p>Use WASD to move the snake, and J to restart if you lose</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Flappy Bird</summary>
    <p>Use J to flap. Also use J to restart if you lose</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Mandelbrot Set</summary>
    <p>There are two modes - iterate mode and zoom mode. You start in iterate mode, and can toggle between them with Select (enter)</p>
    <p>Iterate mode - K to increase iterations, J to decrease</p>
    <p>Zoom mode - WASD to move the view, J to zoom in, K to zoom out</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Julia Set</summary>
    <p>Use WASD to move the seed of the set, J and K to increase and decrease iterations.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Chess</summary>
    <p>Use WASD to move the cursor, and J to select a piece and J to put it down again. To deselect a piece, just try to put it down in an illegal place.</p>
    <p>Note: there is no castling, pawn promotion, or en passant.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Blackjack</summary>
    <p>J to hit, K to stand, up to double down. The game explains it on screen.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Tetris</summary>
    <p>Use A and D to move left and right, W to rotate clockwise, and S to drop. If you lose, press A to restart.</p>
  </details>
  <h2>Hardware and Physical Device</h2>
  <p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Q-nbf0EjklA">Demo on Youtube of finished device</a></p>
  <img src="https://cdn.hackclub.com/019ee35f-67a7-7709-b699-a4260c96196b/PXL_20260620_040404639.jpg" alt="Photo of the physical device, showing the screen and buttons" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .game-instructions {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 400px;
  }
</style>